{
  "summary": "Corrects Doxygen comment syntax across the codebase and enables Clang's `-Wdocumentation-unknown-command` compiler warning in CMake. It escapes literal backslashes in comments, converts standard `/*` comment blocks containing tags into Doxygen `/**` blocks, wraps ASCII diagrams in `@verbatim`, and fixes misspelled or inaccurate `@param` directions.",
  "problem": "Misspelled Doxygen tags (such as `@peer[in]`) and unescaped backslashes in documentation comments are not flagged by Clang's `-Wdocumentation` warning alone. Additionally, Doxygen tags located inside plain `/*` comment blocks are skipped entirely by both Doxygen and compiler diagnostics, leaving documentation mistakes undetected.",
  "evidence": [
    "Commit 2c8c91c5a0 demonstrates that `-Wdocumentation-unknown-command` catches misspelled tags like `@peer[in]` in `src/net_processing.cpp:717` that `-Wdocumentation` alone ignored."
